cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Project Kennel, or cite its threat catalogue or design
  in your own security posture or research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "Project Kennel: kernel-enforced confinement for unsigned code at the user level"
abstract: >-
  A reference monitor for the user level. Kennel runs unvetted code —
  AI coding agents, package postinstall scripts, freshly-cloned
  repositories — under the operator's own account, confined to the
  files, network destinations, and programs a signed policy allows,
  checked one access at a time. Comprises a threat catalogue with
  stable IDs, a substrate-neutral design, and an unprivileged Linux
  runtime composing Landlock, cgroup BPF, seccomp, and namespaces.
authors:
  - family-names: "van Mook"
    given-names: "Remco"
version: "0.7.1"
date-released: "2026-07-17"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://projectkennel.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/projectkennel/projectkennel"
keywords:
  - sandboxing
  - confinement
  - reference monitor
  - AI agents
  - Landlock
  - Linux security
  - least privilege
  - supply chain security
